---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Travel"
  category="About | International Experience"
  year=""
  description="Travel and international experiences shaping Florian Froment's approach to engineering, culture and adaptability."
>

  <p slot="intro" class="hero-intro">
    Travelling has become an important part of the way I learn |
    discovering new environments, cultures and ways of thinking
    constantly reshapes the way I approach engineering and design.
  </p>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      01 | International Mobility
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Learning through immersion.
      </h2>

      <p>
        International experiences have allowed me to leave familiar
        environments and adapt quickly to new academic, professional
        and cultural contexts.
      </p>

      <p>
        Working and studying abroad has strengthened my autonomy,
        communication skills and ability to collaborate with people
        from different backgrounds.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      02 | Poland
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Studying in a different engineering environment.
      </h2>

      <p>
        My academic mobility at the Silesian University of Technology
        in Gliwice gave me the opportunity to experience another
        approach to engineering education.
      </p>

      <p>
        Beyond the technical courses, this experience helped me develop
        greater adaptability and confidence in an international environment.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      03 | Switzerland
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Robotics in an international context.
      </h2>

      <p>
        My internship in Lausanne introduced me to a highly international
        research and innovation environment.
      </p>

      <p>
        Working on robotics projects in Switzerland reinforced my interest
        in research, advanced engineering and cross-disciplinary collaboration.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      04 | Culture
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Understanding places beyond their technology.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Travelling is also a way to observe how architecture,
        transportation, industry and public spaces reflect
        the culture of a place.
      </p>

      <p>
        These differences often influence the way I think about
        usability, design and how technical systems interact
        with their environment.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      05 | Languages
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Communication as part of engineering.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Travelling has reinforced the importance of languages
        in technical and professional environments.
      </p>

      <p>
        Being able to communicate across cultures makes collaboration
        easier and allows engineering ideas to move beyond
        geographical boundaries.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      06 | Perspective
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Changing environment changes perspective.
      </h2>

      <p>
        One of the main reasons I value travel is the ability
        to challenge habits and assumptions.
      </p>

      <p>
        Discovering different ways of living, studying and working
        often reveals solutions or perspectives that would be difficult
        to see while staying in the same environment.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>

</ProjectLayout>
